Runs are now paged, and the same pagination control can be dropped onto any other list.

`Pagination` in `web/src/components/ui/pagination.tsx` takes the current page, page size, total count, and a page-change handler. It shows the range, previous and next buttons, and page numbers, and it stays hidden when everything fits on one page.

```tsx
<Pagination
  page={page}
  pageSize={10}
  total={total}
  onPageChange={setPage}
/>
```

`GET /api/runs` accepts `page` and `pageSize` (default 10, max 50). The response is one page of runs plus `page`, `pageSize`, `total`, and `totalPages`. The active run and the latest saved numbers are still computed from the full history, so the in-progress lock and the start dialog stay correct even when that run is not on the current page.

